# Why this file exists, and why it must not be deleted
#
# `vyloop-customer-web.pages.dev` is an external contract, not an address we
# control. It is encoded in merchant QR codes that are already printed and on
# counters, and it is written into passes that are already in customers' Google
# Wallets. Neither can be redeployed. A pass can be re-issued by reconciliation;
# a printed code cannot be re-issued at all.
#
# The application now deploys as a Worker, so the Pages project has nothing left
# to serve. Left alone it would keep serving its last build — a deployment that
# answers 200 while running code that is no longer this repository. That is
# worse than a 404, because it looks healthy.
#
# So the project is kept alive with exactly one job: hand the old hostname to the
# Worker. This replaces the stale build instead of leaving it behind, and every
# QR code and issued pass keeps working.
#
# The Worker hostname is the destination, not a proxy. New QR codes and new
# passes point at the Worker directly and do not come through here.
#
# This directory carries no `_worker.js` on purpose: a Pages project in advanced
# mode ignores `_redirects` entirely. That is the bug that made `/program` return
# 404 from a build that looked correct on disk, and this file must not repeat it.
#
# Delete this directory and the QR codes die. There is no second chance.

